[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:perform-sensory-evaluation :conduct-sensory-evaluation :assign-quality-grade :finalize-quality-grade-assignment :determine-pass-fail-outcome :finalize-pass-fail-determination :finalize-food-safety-clearance :authorize-food-safety-clearance], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["2799007412-cloud-itonami-isco-7412-electrical-mechanics-fitters-coverage" "2799007514-cloud-itonami-isco-7514-fruit-vegetable-preservers-coverage"], :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["perform the sensory evaluation" "conduct the sensory evaluation" "assign the quality grade" "finalize the quality grade assignment" "finalize the quality-grade assignment" "determine the pass/fail outcome" "determine the pass fail outcome" "finalize the pass/fail determination" "finalize the pass fail determination" "finalize the food-safety clearance" "finalize the food safety clearance" "authorize the food-safety clearance" "authorize the food safety clearance"], :adr/id 2799007515, :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-sample-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-tasting-session :coordinate-supply-order :log-sample-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-anomaly-concern :schedule-tasting-session :coordinate-supply-order :log-sample-record}, :auto #{:schedule-tasting-session :coordinate-supply-order :log-sample-record}}}", :actor/domain :food/tasting-grading-sample-intake-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-sample-record :schedule-tasting-session :flag-anomaly-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:taster-verified :facility-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "7515", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-anomaly-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799007515: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7515 Food and Beverage Tasters and Graders sample-intake-logging/session-scheduling coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7515\n-- Food and Beverage Tasters and Graders** only, Wave3 (production/\ntrades) of the rollout, continuing the batch that already landed\ndozens of the 71xx/72xx/73xx/74xx trades.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7515\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"7515\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Food and Beverage Tasters and\nGraders\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the\nentry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies\n[:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no\nrepository existed at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7515` (`gh\napi` 404 confirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion\nregistry edit promote the `7515` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nFood and Beverage Tasters and Graders perform sensory evaluation and\nquality-grading of food/beverage products -- this is fundamentally a\nquality-decision/food-safety-determination occupation, genuinely\ndifferent from most Wave3 trades: its core function IS making a\npass/fail/grade judgment, so this actor cannot simply \"coordinate,\nnever taste\" as a throwaway phrase -- tasting/grading is the\noccupation's entire purpose. The resolution adopted here: this actor\ncoordinates SAMPLE-INTAKE LOGGING AND SCHEDULING ONLY -- it NEVER\nperforms the sensory evaluation itself (no robot can taste), NEVER\nrecords or proposes a grade/pass-fail determination (that requires a\nhuman taster's sensory judgment, always), and NEVER finalizes a\nfood-safety-clearance decision. The closed op allowlist is limited to\npurely administrative/logistics functions around the human taster's\nwork -- sample intake logging, scheduling tasting sessions, and\nflagging anomalies for the human taster's attention -- never anything\nresembling the taste/grade judgment itself.\n\nNeither `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7514` (Fruit and Vegetable\nPreservers, likely a related food-safety-clearance-exclusion sibling)\nnor `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7511` (Butchers, Fishmongers and\nRelated Food Preparers) existed at scaffold time (`gh api` 404\nconfirmed for both before this actor was built). The reference\nimplementation actually mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance + always-escalate\n-concern + content-based-scope-exclusion safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7412`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7412)\n(Electrical Mechanics and Fitters, same wave, closest available\nstructural reference: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor` split,\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, closed-allowlist +\nalways-escalate concern flag + content-based scope-exclusion with a\nself-trip regression test) -- cloned and read in full in this session.\nA pharmacist-authority-withholding precedent\n(`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-2262`, dispensing gated on\nprior-verification and controlled-substance safety-class, never\nauto-approved) was also reviewed for how a prior actor in this fleet\nhandles an occupation whose core function is itself a human\nprofessional judgment call, informing the \"structurally absent, not\nmerely gated\" resolution adopted below. `cloud-itonami-isco-7514`\nlanded concurrently in this same batch (observed as the most recent\nmerge on `origin/main` when this ADR's worktree was created) but was\nnot available to read at this actor's own scaffold time, so it was not\nused as a reference; it is noted here only as a related sibling\noccupation for future cross-reference.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7515` as an OSS sample-\nintake-logging/session-scheduling coordination actor for food and\nbeverage tasters and graders, following the SAME governed-actor\narchitecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this\nfleet: **Food and Beverage Taster/Grader Advisor asymmetric-gated by\nFoodTasteGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- a different library coordinate from the\n`langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with\nan independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **sample-intake logging and session\nscheduling coordination ONLY, never sensory-evaluation or\nquality-judgment authority** -- it must NEVER be designed to exercise,\nsimulate exercising, or propose exercising the sensory evaluation\nitself, a quality-grade assignment, a pass/fail determination, or a\nfood-safety-clearance decision. These are not merely gated behind\nescalation -- they are structurally absent from the op-allowlist\nentirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-sample-record` -- sample intake/batch-identifier metadata\n  entry (documentation only -- item, timestamp, batch ID -- NEVER a\n  taste/grade/pass-fail outcome)\n- `:schedule-tasting-session` -- human-taster session/panel scheduling\n  proposal\n- `:flag-anomaly-concern` -- surface a sample-condition anomaly (e.g.\n  visible defect, off-odor reported by intake staff) for the human\n  taster's attention, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit-eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- tasting-session supplies (palate\n  cleansers, sample containers) procurement proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles**\nperforming the sensory evaluation itself, assigning or finalizing a\nquality-grade, determining or finalizing a pass/fail outcome, or\nfinalizing or authorizing a food-safety clearance. These are\n**structurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely**, not merely\ngated behind escalation -- an op such as `:assign-quality-grade`\ncannot even be proposed by the reference mock advisor (its\n`infer`/`rationale-for` functions only ever emit one of the four\nallowlist ops), and if any code path (a forged proposal, a future LLM\nadvisor, a misbehaving fork) ever produced such an op, the governor's\nclosed-allowlist HARD check (`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally\nand permanently. A second, independent HARD check\n(`:scope-excluded-action`) names eight concretely-forbidden ops across\nfour scope-exclusion categories (`foodtaste.governor/scope-excluded-\nops`: `:perform-sensory-evaluation`, `:conduct-sensory-evaluation`,\n`:assign-quality-grade`, `:finalize-quality-grade-assignment`,\n`:determine-pass-fail-outcome`, `:finalize-pass-fail-determination`,\n`:finalize-food-safety-clearance`, `:authorize-food-safety-clearance`)\nas defense-in-depth, and is verified by eight dedicated unit tests\n(`foodtaste.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-perform-sensory-\nevaluation`, `.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-conduct-sensory-\nevaluation`, `.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-assign-quality-grade`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-quality-grade-assignment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-determine-pass-fail-outcome`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-pass-fail-determination`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-food-safety-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-food-safety-clearance`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Taster unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered taster record, including certification\n   status (`:no-taster`). Never trusts the proposal's own claim of who\n   the taster is.\n2. **Facility unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an\n   independently registered facility (`:no-facility`). Together with\n   check 1, this directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a\n   taster/facility record must be independently verified/registered\n   (including certification status) before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the eight\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for performing the sensory\n   evaluation, assigning or finalizing a quality grade, determining or\n   finalizing a pass/fail outcome, or finalizing or authorizing a\n   food-safety clearance, is a second HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated unconditionally on content --\n   defense-in-depth on top of the allowlist check: even if a future\n   change somehow widened the allowlist, content-based rejection still\n   independently blocks sensory-evaluation/quality-grade/pass-fail/\n   food-safety-clearance language wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-anomaly-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless\n  of confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a sample-condition\n  anomaly observation -- it never resolves the concern itself, and the\n  robot's role ends at \"here is the anomaly data,\" never \"here is what\n  I recommend doing about this sample's quality.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an\n  over-threshold tasting-supply order is not itself a food-safety\n  determination, unlike a sensory-evaluation, quality-grade,\n  pass-fail-determination, or food-safety-clearance attempt, which is\n  why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft escalate vs.\n  structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"quality\", \"grade\", \"taste\", \"sensory\", \"safety\") can accidentally\nmatch inside the mock advisor's own default rationale text for a\nlegitimate proposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this\nis exactly the risk this vertical's own vocabulary (a sample-intake/\nscheduling coordination actor working adjacent to live food-quality\nwork and human tasters necessarily discusses those concepts to do its\nscheduling/logging job) could trigger if phrased carelessly.\n`foodtaste.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively as\nfinalization/execution ACTIONS across all four scope-exclusion\ncategories (e.g. \"perform the sensory evaluation\", \"assign the\nquality grade\", \"determine the pass/fail outcome\", \"finalize the\nfood-safety clearance\" -- matching the task's own worked example\nphrasing verbatim), never bare nouns, and\n`foodtaste.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-\ntrip-on-scope-exclusion` is a dedicated regression test asserting\nevery op in the closed allowlist, driven through the default mock\nadvisor -- including a deliberately loaded request containing the bare\nnouns \"quality-grade\", \"sensory\" and \"anomaly\"/\"defect\" in its `:item`\nand `:anomaly-type` fields -- never trips `:scope-excluded-action`.\nThe mock advisor's own default rationale template was deliberately\nwritten to contain the bare nouns (\"logged sample intake record for\ntaster ...\", \"scheduled tasting session for sensory evaluation panel\n...\", \"...routed for the human taster's attention\") WITHOUT containing\nany of the full finalization-action phrases, so the regression test is\na genuine stress test of the bare-noun-vs-action-phrase distinction,\nnot a vacuous pass. Green on first run in this session -- the\nscope-exclusion self-trip guard itself was never tripped during\ndevelopment.\n`foodtaste.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-\nconfidence`, `.../holds-a-pass-fail-determination-op-even-at-high-\nconfidence`, `.../holds-a-food-safety-clearance-op-even-at-high-\nconfidence` and `.../holds-a-perform-sensory-evaluation-op-even-at-\nhigh-confidence` additionally exercise the same invariant through the\nfull graph run for each of the four scope-exclusion categories,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7515\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7515` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7515`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit). A dedicated per-occupation `deftest` (race-safe\n  convention for this hot-contention file, several sibling agents\n  landing concurrently this batch) was added asserting `7515`'s\n  maturity/repo/business-id, rather than touching the fragile\n  aggregate `maturity-tier` deftest.\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 29 tests, 64 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy). No mojibake found in any committed source\n  file (`grep -rlP '[\\x{FFFD}]|ï¿½'` returned zero matches).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-quality-grade` or\n  `:approve-food-safety-clearance` that is merely gated behind an\n  always-escalate list (the shape some earlier actors in this fleet\n  use for threshold-gated approvals): rejected outright per the task's\n  explicit domain-design guidance -- an always-escalate op still means\n  the *capability* to finalize a quality-grade/pass-fail/food-safety-\n  clearance decision exists in the code path and is merely deferred to\n  a human gate. For a decision this occupation-defining (the human\n  taster's sensory judgment is the entire purpose of the occupation\n  and is irreplaceable), the capability itself must not exist. The\n  only op related to quality escalation is `:flag-anomaly-concern`,\n  which surfaces the need for the human taster's attention and never\n  itself decides, grades, or defers a quality/food-safety decision for\n  later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring some earlier\n  actors' transaction-amount-ceiling HARD checks): rejected per the\n  task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold tasting-supply\n  order is not itself a food-safety determination, so it is handled as\n  a soft escalate gate, not a hard block; only the sensory-evaluation/\n  quality-grade/pass-fail-determination/food-safety-clearance classes\n  are a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"quality\" \"grade\"\n  \"taste\" \"safety\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip\n  bug class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for\n  this exact task), and per the explicit instruction to phrase\n  scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare\n  nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses quality/\n  grade/taste/safety concepts to do its scheduling/logging job, so a\n  bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the actor's own legitimate\n  proposals (regression-tested directly against rationale/request text\n  that deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Collapsing the four scope-exclusion categories (sensory-evaluation-\n  performance, quality-grade-assignment, pass-fail-determination,\n  food-safety-clearance) into a single generic \"quality-judgment\"\n  op/category: rejected -- CLAUDE.md's CRITICAL section names these as\n  textually distinct finalization/execution actions (\"assign the\n  quality grade\", \"determine the pass/fail outcome\", \"finalize the\n  food-safety clearance\"), and collapsing them would blur the\n  defense-in-depth op-naming and phrase-matching granularity that\n  makes the self-trip regression test a genuine stress test rather\n  than a coincidence; each category also has a semantically distinct\n  real-world referent (physically tasting/smelling/examining a sample\n  vs. assigning a grade label vs. deciding pass/fail vs. clearing a\n  batch for food-safety release) worth naming and testing\n  independently.\n- Merging `taster` and `facility` into a single entity (only checking\n  one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered taster AND independently-registered\n  facility) matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"taster/facility\n  record must be independently verified/registered before any action\"\n  and the established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors\n  with two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-sample-record`** -- sample intake/batch-identifier metadata\n   entry only (item, timestamp, batch ID). Requires an independently\n   registered taster AND facility (`:no-taster`/`:no-facility`). Not a\n   sensory-evaluation, quality-grade, pass-fail-determination, or\n   food-safety-clearance decision in any respect, and NEVER carries a\n   taste/grade/pass-fail outcome field -- no such field exists\n   anywhere in this proposal's shape. It is a records-management\n   action.\n2. **`:schedule-tasting-session`** -- human-taster session/panel\n   scheduling proposal only. Cannot carry a quality-grade/pass-fail\n   decision (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such\n   attempt via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action`\n   content check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any\n   conclusion about a specific sample's quality or food-safety\n   status -- it is a calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-anomaly-concern`** -- surfaces a sample-condition anomaly\n   (visible defect, off-odor reported by intake staff) to the human\n   taster; ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence\n   level, NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through\n   which a condition observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly\n   never resolves, decides, grades, or acts on anything itself -- the\n   human taster reviews and judges entirely on their own sensory\n   authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- tasting-session supplies (palate\n   cleansers, sample containers) procurement proposal only (item,\n   cost). Not a sensory-evaluation, quality-grade, pass-fail-\n   determination, or food-safety-clearance decision of any kind -- it\n   is a purchasing-logistics action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling\n   escalation (above 2000 always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\nperforming the sensory evaluation itself (no robot can taste),\nassigning or finalizing a quality-grade assignment, determining or\nfinalizing a pass/fail outcome, or finalizing or authorizing a\nfood-safety clearance -- these categories are structurally absent, not\ngated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op allowlist itself\n(`foodtaste.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) eight concretely-named\nforbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit level\n(`foodtaste.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`foodtaste.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-perform-sensory-\nevaluation`, `.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-conduct-sensory-\nevaluation`, `.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-assign-quality-grade`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-quality-grade-assignment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-determine-pass-fail-outcome`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-pass-fail-determination`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-food-safety-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-food-safety-clearance`), and\n(c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`foodtaste.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against rationale\ntext that attempts to assign the quality grade, determine the\npass/fail outcome, or finalize the food-safety clearance even via an\notherwise-allowlisted op\n(`foodtaste.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-assign-\nthe-quality-grade-even-with-allowlisted-op`, `.../hard-on-scope-\nexcluded-rationale-determine-the-pass-fail-outcome-even-with-\nallowlisted-op`, `.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-finalize-\nthe-food-safety-clearance`). The human taster's sensory judgment is\nirreplaceable and this actor never touches it, at any layer, in any\ndisposition path.", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}", :test/counts "{:total 29, :assertions 64, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Food and Beverage Tasters and Graders Sample-Intake Coordination Practice", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :taster-verification :facility-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7515", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7515", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7515], :test/simulator :foodtaste.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7515 — Food and Beverage Tasters and Graders Sample-Intake/Scheduling Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7515}]
